Neural Networks and Spatial Intelligence are core models for solving generalized AI problems, with increasing applications in many areas of society, such as scene understanding, autonomous driving, and large models. This course leads a deep dive into algorithmic models with deep learning at their core to solve general-purpose problems in AI, especially the spatial inteligence, such as image recognition, target detection, image segmentation; and extends to 3D deep learning. The course uses PyTorch as a working environment for practice and problem solving, and introduces the latest cutting-edge advances in neural networks and deep learning. The total number of classroom hours is 54, and the course meets for 5 hours per week in weeks 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, and 14, and for 3 hours in week 16.
The course starts with an introduction to the basics of neural networks and deep learning, learns the contents of current advanced artificial intelligence technologies, and guides students to complete the corresponding experimental tasks through groups.

1) Basic knowledge: including machine learning overview, linear regression model, multilayer perceptual machine, convolutional neural network, recurrent neural network, network optimization and regularization, self-attention mechanism, self-supervised learning, generative deep learning, sequence generation model;
2) Advanced Artificial Intelligence Techniques: including generative models (AIGC), grand models (GPT), diffusion models (Diffusion Model), autonomous driving, 3D Gaussian splatting, etc;
3) Deep learning techniques: network training and optimization, case study of combining deep learning with autonomous driving in the industrial field.
4) Experimental tasks: focusing on the cultivation of hands-on practical ability, according to students' personal interests and future career planning, encourage students to complete their own group. With the help of hardware server clusters such as the college's cloud computing experimental platform and big data testing ground, students can complete basic knowledge practical tasks and course projects. At the same time, students are encouraged to combine advanced artificial intelligence technology to propose the reimplementation and improvement of existing tasks, and realize the sorting of algorithms to form an English paper with architecture.
